      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start, but it's a bit too brief. The senior investigators usually need more granular detail to feel confident about the report. \n\nCan you expand on this? Try to make it more technical. You can include specific part identifiers, subsystem error codes (like AX-1024, BK-9932, etc.), or sensor readings to flesh out the description. Just please, keep it readable and make sure it sounds like a real incident report, not just a string of technical gibberish. I really need this to pass the human review.",
