    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's an expanded version of the technical summary:\n\nChain Number: [Insert Chain Number, not needed in this case]\nProvider ID: N90-42\nEngine Model: Turbofan X-15 \nDepartment: [Insert Department, APU, FP, etc.]\n\nA pre-flight inspection of the N90-42 with Turbofan model X-15 engine revealed two notable technical issues. The secondary cooling shroud, specifically part number ABR-765 (AS1280), exhibited a hairline crack, at a point of maximum tensile stress. This finding prompted a detailed examination of the area between the cooling shroud's attachment flanges (subsystem error code AX-1221) and the associated ductwork. Visual inspection using thermal imaging (Thermal camerA14FL ppt) confirmed localized thermal irregularities, suggesting temperature differences between adjacent surface areas.\n\nIn addition, minor oil seepage was identified near the ACES (Actuator) housing, specifically chamber AXSK-6039 (Series II). This finding may relate to bearing clearance issues or leverage stresses on the surrounding housing (BK-6341). The area was examined under bright light, using a magnification of x50, and photographed for further analysis.\n\nSubsystem sensor",
      "source": "target",
